-- =========================================================================
-- Syntax — the surface expression ADT (sugars intact). expr-substrate
-- Phase 1 (brief:
-- `workstreams/expr-substrate/briefs/phase-1-register-syntax-expr.md`).
--
-- `Syntax` is what the parser produces (post Phase 4 re-layer); it is a
-- SUPERSET of `Expr` (`fenel/std/expr.fenel`): the seven core mirrors plus
-- the four surface sugars that `desugar : Syntax -> Expr` (Phase 2) lowers
-- away. Two ADTs, two registered entities, two files — concatenating `.fenel`
-- files breaks parsing, so `Syntax` lives apart from `Expr` and each loads
-- separately in `type-foundation.ts`'s pass.
--
-- The 14 cases:
--   • 7 core mirrors:  SLit / SVar / SCall / SLambda / SMatch / SConstruct
--                      / SRecord  (the `Expr` shapes, S-prefixed)
--   • 4 surface sugars: SIf  (cond / then / else)
--                       SLet (bindings / body)
--                       SDo  (exprs)
--                       SOp  (op / operands — one case covers binary AND unary
--                             infix; the operator fnId + its operand list,
--                             resolved via Infixable / Prefixable at desugar)
--   • 1 surface sugar:  SWhere (body / bindings — REALIZED, fenel-surface-
--                       extensions Phase 4; the anticipated additive case)
--   • 1 surface sugar:  SMethod (cls / method / args — REALIZED, fenel-surface-
--                       extensions Phase 6; a module-qualified-method head)
--   • 1 surface form:   SAnn (expr / type — REALIZED, modules-as-values Phase
--                       2d; a type annotation `(e : T)`)
--
-- where-clauses LANDED (fenel-surface-extensions Phase 4) as the additive
-- `SWhere body: a bindings: a` case — a function-level `where` (`body where h =
-- …`) is a distinct expression FORM (unlike guards, an arm field), so it is a
-- real Syntax case. `bindings` is a LIST `[{name, value}]` (the SAME shape
-- `SLet.bindings` uses), so `desugar (SWhere body binds)` ≡ `desugar (SLet binds
-- body)` (scoped-let — `where` is sugar for `let`) and the JSON-Logic WIRE shape
-- stays the oracle's `{where:[body, {name: value, …}]}` (the list→object is
-- Syntax-internal, invisible at the `{where}` boundary). NO `Expr` change —
-- `where` desugars to `let` (an applied-`ELambda` in the 7-case core), so `Expr`
-- stays at 7. GUARDS LANDED (fenel-surface-extensions Phase 3) WITHOUT an ADT
-- change: `SMatch.arms` is the untyped `a` slot, and a guard is represented as an
-- OPTIONAL `guard` FIELD on the arm record (`{pattern, guard, body}`, D1 option A
-- — a guard is an arm condition, not a pattern). Guard-free arms keep the bare
-- `{pattern, body}`.
--
-- qualified-method references LANDED (fenel-surface-extensions Phase 6) as the
-- additive `SMethod cls: String method: String args: a` case — an application
-- whose HEAD is a dotted ident with an UPPERCASE class segment + a LOWER-initial
-- method segment (`Foldable.foldr g z xs`, bare `Foldable.foldr`) is a distinct
-- expression FORM (NOT an SCall — its runtime semantics are reflective typeclass-
-- /module-method DISPATCH, not a named call; NOT an SConstruct). `cls` + `method`
-- are separate `String` fields and `args` the lowered-arg list — the exact shape
-- the wire `{method:[cls, method, …args]}` flattens to (`syntaxToJsonLogic`
-- prepends cls+method then spreads args; the adapter `jlsMethod` does the
-- inverse). `desugar (SMethod cls m args)` ⇒ the dotted-fnId core form `ECall
-- (cls ++ "." ++ method) args` — NO `Expr` change (Expr stays at 7; the locked
-- Expr has no EMethod case, the desugar.fenel header's documented stance). The
-- PRODUCTION (interpreted) path evaluates the wire `{method}` reflectively
-- (json-logic.ts methodOp); the COMPILE path is a ledgered fence-for-now (the
-- dotted-fnId resolution is P4/P8's; zero corpus files compile a `{method}`
-- body) — the guards' D2 precedent, distinct from `where`'s supported compile.
--
-- type annotations LANDED (modules-as-values Phase 2d, amending D-C) as the
-- additive `SAnn expr: a type: a` case — the surface `( Expr : Type )` (one
-- colon, one parenthesised expression; `::` stays a reserved, unparseable
-- token). `type` is the written FenelType, carried OPAQUELY (it is `$`-keyed,
-- so a `.fenel` body passes it through, never inspects it). The wire is the
-- existing `{ann: [e, T]}` node. `desugar` REJECTS an SAnn over an SMethod
-- (erasing that annotation would change which instance runs — the written
-- type selects it) and is transparent otherwise; inference infers the
-- expression and never returns the written type unchecked.
--
-- TYPING DISCIPLINE (brief decision 5): mirrors `CoreExpr`/`Expr` — precise
-- `String` for `name` / `fnId` / `ctor` / `op`, loose untracked `a` for every
-- recursive / payload slot. `a` is a free type variable (no head param).
-- SConstruct carries the `fields` slot (named-field metadata), same delta as
-- `EConstruct`.
--
-- Registered codeName = `Syntax`. P1 registers the ADT only — the parser does
-- NOT start emitting `Syntax` here (brief decision 6): that swap lands with its
-- consumers (`desugar` P2, the compiler-entry re-layer P4). Authored via the
-- Ext-1 entity-facet path, threaded through `type-foundation.ts`'s load pass.
-- =========================================================================

@entity
@label "Syntax"
@description "The surface expression ADT — what the parser produces, sugars intact. Superset of Expr: the 7 core mirrors (SLit / SVar / SCall / SLambda / SMatch / SConstruct / SRecord) plus 6 surface sugars desugar lowers away and the annotation form — SIf (cond/then/else), SLet (bindings/body), SDo (exprs), SOp (op/operands, one case for binary + unary infix resolved via Infixable), SWhere (body/bindings — a function-level `where`, sugar for let), SMethod (cls/method/args — a module-qualified-method head `Foldable.foldr`, dispatches reflectively; desugars to a dotted-fnId ECall), SAnn (expr/type — a type annotation `(e : T)`, the wire `{ann: [e, T]}`; the type is an opaque FenelType; desugar rejects it over an SMethod, else erases it). Guards are an arm field (not a case). where-clauses LANDED (Phase 4); qualified-method refs LANDED (Phase 6); annotations LANDED (modules-as-values Phase 2d)."
Syntax a =
  SLit value: a
  | SVar name: String
  | SCall fnId: String args: a
  | SLambda params: a body: a
  | SMatch scrutinee: a arms: a
  | SConstruct ctor: String args: a fields: a
  | SRecord fields: a
  | SIf cond: a then: a else: a
  | SLet bindings: a body: a
  | SDo exprs: a
  | SOp op: String operands: a
  | SWhere body: a bindings: a
  | SMethod cls: String method: String args: a
  | SAnn expr: a type: a
